# .env.example — environment variable template
#
# dsh-redmark needs NO API key and NO secret to work.
# This file only documents the data-directory variable used for local testing
# and external scripts. Copy to .env for local development only; never commit
# a real .env (see .gitignore).

# ---- Data directory (optional) ----
# Host writes the bookmark store and diagnostic log under this directory.
# Priority: DSH_HOME > os.homedir()/.dsh
# Defaults (when unset):
#   Windows:   C:\Users\<you>\.dsh\dsh-redmark.json
#              C:\Users\<you>\.dsh\dsh-redmark-trace.log
#   macOS/Linux: ~/.dsh/dsh-redmark.json
#                ~/.dsh/dsh-redmark-trace.log
# Normally you do not need to set this; DSH injects it at startup.
# DSH_HOME=./.dsh

# ---- Notes ----
# The primary bookmark copy lives in browser localStorage (per session).
# The Host /dsh-redmark endpoint is a best-effort durability mirror:
#   - when the endpoint is unavailable, bookmarks still work via localStorage;
#   - when available, writes are mirrored to the JSON above for recovery.
# Bookmarks saved by the older "Session Bookmarks" bundle are migrated
# automatically on first read (legacy localStorage keys and legacy JSON file).
# The trace log is plain text, containing only structured jump/guard metrics —
# no conversation text and no secrets.
